title One error name, two ceilings
prompt THE BATON -- pheromone's lane: Glow runes and their lowering, the stdlib, the value model, and the seams where one module's meaning reaches another
think Round open read HEAD 1442838c6d clean. A stale hot scoped pass from launch_head f6eee0f3b2 held the roster lock with its verdict already fixed at tree_moved; I resolved pid 956114 through /proc to this tree, TERMed it by the runner's own instruction, then relaunched cold with --cadence-slice 1.
think My rung three reads make refusal output stable -- field, value, ceiling, unit, reason. The contract's Bounds and refusals sentence asks for exactly those five where a ceiling applies and field plus reason where none does. Glow answered every refusal with a bare Zig error value, which carries a class and no measurement.
think Rota row 3, Water, care and flow. The row reads by swallowing rather than at a distance, so I opened glow/rune_shape.rye and read the refusing lines themselves rather than its doc comment. That closeness is what found the real fault.
think glow/rune_shape.rye:492 refuses a fourth payload face with error.TooManyFields -- the SAME name the nine-face tuple ceiling returns three call sites up. Two different ceilings, two different units, one word. The face name, the running count and the ceiling all stood in locals the return threw away.
think I checked absence properly: path_absence_scan read all three paths absent here and upstream, commits_behind=0, and the live claim board carried no overlapping path. I opened the claim, committed it, and pushed before writing a line of the build.
think Then the guard found what the check could not. rye_compiled_reach printed its uncompiled bodies in the hot pass and tally/receipt_refusal.rye and mantra/src/receipt_refusal_witness.rye stood in the list beside mine -- a peer's record, landed at 4914d0721 the evening before, with the same five parts and the same rendering.
think That is REDS 715's shape exactly: no shared path, no shared name, one subject. The absence instrument was right and the claim board was right, and neither could reach a file whose name shares nothing with mine.
think Reading the peer's design made the call easy. Its Measure is an optional struct holding value, ceiling and unit together, so a ceiling applies is structural; my first draft carried a has_ceiling bool beside three loose fields, which is the braid single-stranded.md names. Theirs is better and it landed first.
think So I rebuilt mine as its peer rather than beside it -- same Measure shape, same render, same kebab word idiom -- with Glow's own vocabulary of two units and two reasons. Two records rather than one, because a Glow parse refusal is not a receipt admission refusal and borrowing unsuitable_value_unit would braid the language into the product.
think Two records rendering one line is one rule written twice, so the witness greps both format strings out of both files and asserts each stands exactly once in each. That agreement is checked rather than claimed, and prefixing my line with a head word reds it.
think The row's dual seat named the threading move: diverge by strengthening, not rewriting. parse_source_reporting accretes beside parse_source, which keeps its published bytes and calls the new entry with a scratch slot it drops. Leg nine proves that rather than the sentence.
obs The mutation that mattered was collapsing too_many_payload_faces back into too_many_fields. Leg seven reds on it, which means the record is genuinely what tells the two ceilings apart rather than a decoration over an error name that already did.
obs A guard's ordinary output found what two purpose-built coordination instruments could not. rye_compiled_reach was reporting a ratchet it has been over for a long time, and its list happened to name my subject in a peer's spelling. Reading a red's whole output rather than only its verdict is what made the difference.
obs rye_compiled_reach cannot see a .rish witness that builds through run sh -c rye_build.sh, so glow/face_lit_witness.rye, glow/expr_witness.rye and glow/rune_shape_witness.rye all read uncompiled while rostered witnesses compile each one every lap. It stood at 799 before my lap and reads 800 after.
rota lap 5073, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; growing-a-language.md's fourth move, diverge by strengthening rather than rewriting, is what shaped parse_source_reporting accreting beside an entry whose bytes stand
